From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:22:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 246/342] app_server: colour emoji (fonts with colour pictures)

A font whose glyphs are colour pictures (CBDT, sbix: Noto Color Emoji)
was drawn as nothing: FreeType doesn't scale them, so FT_Set_Pixel_Sizes
failed for every size but the font's one (109 pixels), and the glyphs
were never loaded in colour.

FontEngine now picks such a font's size closest above ours with
FT_Select_Size, loads glyphs with FT_LOAD_COLOR, and keeps a colour
glyph as premultiplied B_RGBA32 pixels (glyph_data_color) scaled to
our size with a tent filter (averaging when shrinking, interpolating
when growing). Colour layers FreeType draws itself (COLR) take the
same way. AGGTextRenderer draws them through the clipping region and
the alpha mask: over the destination in B_OP_COPY, B_OP_OVER and
B_OP_ALPHA (with the high colour's alpha), as a shape in the high colour
in the other modes. Rotated, sheared or scaled text gets them upright
and in the font's size.

"Noto Color Emoji" comes before "Noto Emoji" in the fallbacks, and a
colour font is asked first for the characters that are emoji by default
(Unicode's Emoji_Presentation below U+1F000, everything a colour font
has from U+1F000 on), even when the font or an earlier fallback has
them in black and white (Noto Sans Symbols has U+2615 HOT BEVERAGE,
U+2B50 WHITE MEDIUM STAR and some 200 more). A variation selector after
a character asks for the other look: U+FE0F colour, U+FE0E black and
white; the glyph cache keeps such a glyph apart (kGlyphCodeEmoji,
kGlyphCodeText). FreeType needs libpng for the pictures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
